From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] glm tests: the disk ranks rig sets the head flag snapshots.bytes reads

patches/engine/0028 adds Engine.head with no default and makes cuda_snapshots.bytes count the MTP head's
rows only when it is set. The PR's cuda_disk_ranks_test Rig makes a real Engine with a.create, which applies
no field defaults, and sets mtp but never head, so bytes read an undefined bool: the blank state's lease
left the head rows out and 'a blank state takes bytes past its words and front only once sealed' failed
at seal (cuda_snapshots.zig:149, error.SnapshotSize: its mtp_len at - 1 needs them). The rig's engine is
one whose head absorbs, as the PR's tests assume, so head is true.
---

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_disk_ranks_test.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_disk_ranks_test.zig
index 08ac674e864626e81f06989ae15d22d12b0798ad..6f6a3666fc069c68135474d24a0711dcecd09800 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_disk_ranks_test.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_disk_ranks_test.zig
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ const Rig = struct {
         e.cur = &x.seq;
         e.capacity = fixture.capacity;
         e.mtp = true;
+        e.head = true; // the head absorbs: a blank state's lease counts the head rows seal's mtp_len takes
         e.slot = 0;
         e.stream = .{ .d = &x.d, .handle = null };
         e.m.glue.put_words = .{ .d = &x.d, .handle = null };
